"How did the central field at {#} cm compare with the one at {#} cm, and with what you expected in Before the lab {#}? Use the Ampère’s law argument of Before the lab {#} to explain why the radius has the effect it does, and why a single loop behaves differently. Then: an MRI magnet makes {#} T inside a long winding. How many ampere turns per meter does that need, and why are such magnets superconducting?",
