"Treat the solenoid as loops packed \\(n\\) per meter: the slice of winding between \\(z'\\) and \\(z' + dz'\\) is a loop carrying \\(nI\\,dz'\\). Integrate the loop formula over the length of the winding, using \\(\\int R^2\\,du/(R^2+u^2)^{3/2} = u/\\sqrt{R^2+u^2}\\), to show that the field at the center is \\(\\mu_0 nI\\,L/\\sqrt{L^2+4R^2}\\), and find the field at an end. Compare both with your Part {#} row for {#} turns in {#} cm.",
